WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:06.608
Installing PageMotor on GoDaddy. The install itself is standard cPanel, about ten minutes.

2
00:00:06.608 --> 00:00:11.808
But GoDaddy differs from other hosts in three ways worth knowing before you start,

3
00:00:11.808 --> 00:00:15.296
and one of them decides whether you can install at all.

4
00:00:15.996 --> 00:00:25.398
That one is the product. PageMotor needs GoDaddy's Linux Web Hosting plan, the one whose dashboard shows a cPanel Admin button.

5
00:00:25.398 --> 00:00:34.429
Two popular GoDaddy products cannot run PageMotor at all: Websites + Marketing, their site builder, and Managed WordPress.

6
00:00:34.429 --> 00:00:43.164
Neither gives you cPanel or file access, so there is nowhere to put the files. Check that first, before anything else.

7
00:00:43.864 --> 00:00:55.464
Then the ordinary part. Run the preflight check, then open cPanel, File Manager, and the folder for your site, which for your main domain is public_html.

8
00:00:55.464 --> 00:01:00.013
Upload the PageMotor zip, right-click it and choose Extract.

9
00:01:00.013 --> 00:01:09.870
If Extract stalls partway, just run it again: GoDaddy's shared servers sometimes pause big jobs, and a retry normally finishes it.

10
00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:16.672
The database uses cPanel's MySQL Database Wizard, which does the whole job in one pass.

11
00:01:16.672 --> 00:01:24.108
Name it, create the user, let the generator make the password, and on the last screen tick ALL PRIVILEGES.

12
00:01:24.108 --> 00:01:33.577
Here is the GoDaddy difference: unlike most cPanel hosts, GoDaddy usually shows the name exactly as you typed it, with no prefix added.

13
00:01:33.577 --> 00:01:41.713
But the name has to be unique across GoDaddy's whole system, so something plain like pagemotor may already be taken.

14
00:01:41.713 --> 00:01:47.676
Use something distinctive, and copy the final names exactly as the wizard shows them.

15
00:01:48.376 --> 00:02:01.048
Then rename config-sample.php to exactly config.php, which is the step that switches PageMotor on, and put your three values in. DB_HOST stays localhost.

16
00:02:01.048 --> 00:02:12.478
Ignore any older tutorial telling you to hunt for a special GoDaddy MySQL host name: that advice is for their long-retired legacy hosting.

17
00:02:13.178 --> 00:02:21.510
Then go straight to /admin/. On that first visit PageMotor sets itself up and walks you into creating your admin user.

18
00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:25.252
Open the admin before you open the front of the site.

19
00:02:25.952 --> 00:02:31.287
Now the part where GoDaddy genuinely differs, and it is worth two minutes.

20
00:02:31.287 --> 00:02:38.064
GoDaddy's shared hosting blocks outbound SMTP to outside mail services, as a matter of policy.

21
00:02:38.064 --> 00:02:49.526
Mailgun, SendGrid, Brevo and the rest will simply time out, on every port. So the advice you see everywhere else, just point it at Mailgun, does not work here.

22
00:02:49.526 --> 00:03:01.061
And the giveaway is the shape of the failure: a timeout, rather than a rejected password. The connection never reaches the provider, so it is not your settings.

23
00:03:01.761 --> 00:03:11.807
What does work is GoDaddy's own mail system. In your mail plugin, set the host to localhost, port 25, no encryption and no authentication,

24
00:03:11.807 --> 00:03:21.635
because the server trusts mail sent from itself. Or pick the PHP mail() transport, which uses the same thing with nothing to configure.

25
00:03:21.635 --> 00:03:29.207
And skip the old relay hostname you will find quoted online; it is deprecated, and it tends to time out.

26
00:03:29.907 --> 00:03:35.828
One more thing, because it catches people out. “Sent” is not the same as “delivered”.

27
00:03:35.828 --> 00:03:45.929
Your GoDaddy box will happily report the mail as sent, and Gmail and Outlook will quietly bin it, because the domain has no SPF and DKIM records.

28
00:03:45.929 --> 00:03:53.870
It does not bounce. It just disappears. Add those two DNS records for your domain and real inboxes will accept it.

29
00:03:54.570 --> 00:04:05.370
And if something does break: on GoDaddy an error_log file does not appear in your site folder by itself, so look under cPanel, Metrics, Errors instead.

30
00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:12.093
A 500 or a blank page is almost always config.php: wrong name, wrong folder, or never renamed.

31
00:04:12.093 --> 00:04:20.390
“MySQLi Connection Error” is better news, because it means config.php is working and PageMotor reached the database.

